    {
      "ports": [],
      "tags": [],
      "id": "patches",
      "kind": "storage",
      "label": "vLLM patches",
      "sublabel": "8 vendored patches, applied to the INSTALLED package",
      "note": "Applied to site-packages, not a source checkout. Nothing records that they are applied — RE-APPLY AFTER ANY pip install, upgrade or venv rebuild.\n\nvllm-pr48375-mamba-prefix-eagle.patch GATES prefix caching (see the flag on this node).\nvllm-pr50021-gdn-spec-bounds.patch makes concurrent MTP requests safe, so --max-num-seqs 8 is fine.\n\nCheck: patch -p2 --dry-run --forward < the patch. \"Reversed (or previously applied)\" means applied.\nDocumented in deploy/profiles/ENGINE-PATCHES.md.",
      "frame": "engine",
      "status": "done",
      "position": {
        "x": 2716,
        "y": 60
      },
      "flags": [
        {
          "id": "f1",
          "kind": "issue",
          "title": "A vLLM reinstall silently un-gates prefix caching",
          "note": "PREFIX_CACHE=1 in the unit is only correct while vllm-pr48375-mamba-prefix-eagle.patch is applied to the installed package. The patches live in site-packages, so any pip install, upgrade or venv rebuild removes them — and nothing in the venv, the unit, the panel or the logs records that they are gone. The engine starts happily and serves wrong output: a cached page whose recurrent-state snapshot was taken over rejected MTP draft tokens gets reused, producing wrong tool calls and degraded long-context answers with no error anywhere. The failure is invisible by construction, which is what makes it worth a flag rather than a comment.",
          "fix": "Add a patch check to the Core unit's ExecStartPre: dry-run each patch in ~/qwen-serving/patches and fail the unit unless every one reports \"Reversed (or previously applied)\". A Core that will not start is a better outcome than one that lies. Until that exists, ENGINE-PATCHES.md carries the manual check and the rule: no 48375, no prefix caching.",
          "by": "agent",
          "at": "2026-09-04T19:53:33.418Z"
        }
      ]
    },
